  "protocol": "Stratified 5-fold (StratifiedGroupKFold: identical feature vectors share a fold) repeated over seeds [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]; scaler inside the per-fold pipeline; engineered features are deterministic row-wise formulas (nothing is fitted, so no leakage). Metrics are out-of-fold, mean \u00b1 std over seeds; confusion matrices are summed over seeds. RAW-DEDUP drops exact duplicate rows and keeps conflicting labels (test labels are the untouched originals; this is the headline). CONFLICT-RESOLVED relabels identical vitals by majority vote (ties to the higher risk class); it also cleans the TEST labels, so it is easier and shown for transparency, not as a headline. NAIVE keeps all 1014 rows and duplicates, which leaks.",
  "selection_rule": "Among model \u00d7 feature-set combinations on the raw-dedup protocol: highest mean High-risk recall among those with High precision >= 0.60 and macro-F1 within 0.05 of the best; ties within 0.01 recall go to higher macro-F1.",
